From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Modrinth Enhanced <patches@modrinth-enhanced.invalid>
Date: Fri, 18 Sep 2026 00:03:21 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Offer the launchers instances can be imported from

Importing only listed the launchers that were found and had instances.
Anyone whose launcher sits somewhere else, or who has not installed it
where the launcher usually goes, was left with an empty list and a path
to type in by hand.

Every launcher the importers read is offered now, installed or not:
Prism Launcher, MultiMC, PolyMC, ATLauncher, GDLauncher and CurseForge,
each with the folder it keeps its instances in on this system, Flatpak
and macOS bundles included. Picking one reads that folder; with nothing
there, its path lands in the field to be corrected. PolyMC and other
MultiMC forks are read by Prism's importer, so the name shown and the
importer used are no longer the same thing.

The initials in a badge tell the entries apart without carrying anyone
else's logo around.
